SUMMARY:Women Who Took a Stand
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260521T193000
UID:d11b24f86a3199124ca5ef1ec55cfbe1@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Presentation\, Tweens\, Teens\, Adults\, Seniors\n\nWhether it
  was spies\, stay at home mothers\, wives\, activists\, nurses\, soldiers\
 , or working behind the scenes\, women have always taken action. This was 
 the case during the Civil War. While many thought a women's place was at h
 ome raising children\, instead\, women of all ages and backgrounds took ac
 tion.Join Civil War Historian Cindy Beaston as she discusses some of the w
 omen who defied societal norms and fought for the very rights we hold dear
  today.All are welcome to attend.
LOCATION:Columbia\, COL Meeting Room
