DESCRIPTION:Storytime\, Toddlers\, Children\, Adults\n\nBring the whole fa
 mily to the library for a delightful storytime experience! Perfect for chi
 ldren ages 0-12\, this program features engaging stories\, lively songs\, 
 and fun activities designed to spark a love of reading and learning. This 
 is a wonderful opportunity for families to bond\, build literacy skills\, 
 and create lasting memories together!Adults attending with their child(ren
 ) do NOT need to register. Please add any additional registrants to your r
 egistration if more than one child that will be participating in the progr
 am.Registration will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, May 13th for Manheim To
 wnship and East Lampeter residents and on Friday\, May 15th for residents 
 of other municipalities.Storytime PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to c
 ancel their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will 
 be restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one mon
 th’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to th
 e start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notifi
 ed of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 
 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and othe
 r circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. A
 t this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who wi
 ll be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the
  program. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program
  5 minutes past the start time.Accompanying Adults – This program is for
  adults and children to enjoy together. Please plan to attend and be engag
 ed with your child. Drop offs will not be permitted.Cancellations- Please 
 check your email prior to departing to verify that the program has not bee
 n cancelled.
