SUMMARY:Young Writers' Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260611T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260611T170000
UID:1bb43f55d137f96c6f5bcd56286d761c@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Virtual\, Children\, Tweens\n\nHybrid program
 -please register.  Entering grades K through 5. Adult caregivers should pl
 an to attend at least the first session to understand the program which is
  self-guided with adult assistance when needed!Join a group of writers thi
 s summer! We'll meet once per month to share our successes\, keep each oth
 er accountable\, and talk about some writing strategies.Kids write indepen
 dently and meet once per month as a group to discuss our goals\, progress\
 , and challenges. On July 1\, we'll begin to write our very own novels!  A
 ugust is an optional meeting for any writers who wish to share their succe
 ss with a little party!Registration is intended for the entire session so 
 please just register for the first session - even if you are starting a bi
 t late. Once we begin writing our novels in July\, the group will not be a
 ccepting new writers. Vacations can be easily accommodated with this progr
 am as we are working on an online platform and all meetings are hybrid!
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL Story Corner/Early Literacy Lab
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/young-writers-program-17
 0241
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
