BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-summerzine-1st-session-160122"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Teen SummerZine - 1st Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T143000
UID:e7bce5a5f93a1795d69d17d659a8d609@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Virtual\, Tweens\, Teens\n\nThe Teen Summer Zi
 ne is back for 2026\, with a new lineup of mentor authors and artists\, ne
 w locations\, and a celebration of the hand-made roots of zines! All Lanca
 ster County teens are welcome to participate. Students ages 12-19 will lea
 rn from local arts professionals while creating their own hand-made public
 ations that can include comics\, fan art and fan fiction\, poetry\, collag
 e\, and illustrations. All art and writing materials will be provided\, al
 ong with snacks! Students may submit their favorite pieces for publication
  into a county-wide digital zine that will be available for checkout throu
 gh Libby at the end of the summer.  The first session of this program will
  be offered both in person and via Zoom. Zoom link: https://us02web.zoom.u
 s/j/82312607281?pwd=1yzWtpn6ba2OMPtyft2EB7BtMawaan.1Sessions will take pla
 ce at the following times and locations: Saturday\, June 13\, 1pm. Manheim
  Township Library: Create Comics with graphic novelist Jamar Nicholas. Man
 heim Township Public Library is excited to host the first session of this 
 popular countywide program just for teens! Participants will meet acclaime
 d graphic novelist Jamar Nicholas and explore how art and storytelling com
 e together in the creation of a zine. Teens will have the opportunity to s
 ubmit their own artwork and stories\, which will be compiled into a collab
 orative teen-created magazine.Saturday\, June 27\, 12:30pm. Ephrata Librar
 y: Make a FanZine with Lancaster Zine Fest's Louise LoBello. Saturday\, Ju
 ly 11\,12:30pm. Ephrata Library: Create Collage Poetry with author and poe
 t Lindsay Bandy. Saturday\, July 25\, 1pm. Quarryville Library: Make Zine 
 Art with local artist Ciana Malchione. Registration will open at 9:00AM on
  Wednesday\, May 13th\, 2026. LIBRARY PROGRAM POLICIES:Drop Off Program 
 – This program is intended for children over the age of 13 years who can
  participate independently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child wit
 h youth services staff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the
  event space. Designated Ages – Please adhere to the age restrictions de
 signated on your registration. Only children in that age range will be adm
 itted.Registration Requirements –  To help us manage our space\, please 
 register every person who will be attending\, including siblings.No Show 
 – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library p
 rograms in a month will be restricted from registering for future programs
  for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at l
 east 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the w
 aiting list to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arr
 ivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to al
 low for parking and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly a
 t the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those
  on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants
  may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permit
 ted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-summerzine-1st-sess
 ion-160122
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-zine-175955"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Teen Zine
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260613T143000
UID:bc3dbdcddc66a8b36e6151f869106913@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Teens\n\nNOTE: THIS PROGRAM IS BEING OFFERED LIVE AT MANHEIM T
 OWNSHIP PUBLIC LIBRARY AND ALSO VIRTUALLY. YOU MAY PARTICIPATE LIVE OR FRO
 M YOUR HOME BY REGISTERING THROUGH THEIR EVENT CALENDAR. IF YOU WOULD LIKE
  TO USE OUR LAPTOPS AT QUARRYVILLE LIBRARY PLEASE REGISTER HERE (REQUIRES 
 A LIBRARY CARD WITH DIGITAL ACCESS!)Lindsay Bandy Lindsay Bandy writes poe
 try\, fiction\, and nonfiction for teens\, including the 2024 Carolyn W. F
 ield Honor-winning novel “Inevitable Fate.” She has worked in public a
 nd school libraries\, served in various roles with the Society of Children
 ’s Book Writers and Illustrators\, and teaches writing classes for stude
 nts of all ages. She lives in Lancaster County with her husband\, two daug
 hters\, two cats\, and a growing collection of houseplants.Lindsay is the 
 creator of the Teen Summer Zine program and will be hosting each session. 
 Jamar Nicholas Jamar Nicholas is an award-winning\, Philadelphia-based art
 ist and educator\, dedicating his career to helping young people realize t
 he power of visual narrative. He has taught and lectured on the topic of c
 omics creation at numerous institutions\, dedicating his career to empower
 ing young people to create their own cartoons and comics.Jamar aims to bri
 ng awareness to anti-bullying\, healing\, positive images of people of col
 or\, the idea that everyone can be a hero\, channeled through images and a
 rt of the every-person archetype.
LOCATION:Quarryville
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-zine-175955
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
