BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/lego-block-party-172194"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Lego Block Party!
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260615T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260615T190000
UID:e56052e6a4b8b0471898c14796c26ab6@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nRegistration for 
 Lego Block Party will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 3rd for Manheim T
 ownship and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, June 10th for resid
 ents of other municipalities.For youth ages 8-12 years of age only.The LEG
 O Block Party at the library is a fun and creative program where children 
 ages 8-12 come together to build various creations using LEGO bricks. Part
 icipants often have the opportunity to work individually or in teams to de
 sign and construct imaginative structures\, vehicles\, and scenes based on
  a theme or their own imagination. The club typically fosters collaboratio
 n\, problem-solving\, and fine motor skills while encouraging a love for b
 uilding and creativity. It's a great way for community members to socializ
 e\, learn\, and have fun in a supportive environment.Library Program Polic
 iesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more than 
 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registering for futu
 re programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registr
 ations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow for tho
 se on the waiting list to be notified of their change in registration stat
 us.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the pr
 ogram to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program will begin
  promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeit
 ed to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, 
 registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will no
 t be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Check In
  - All participants must provide an emergency contact number upon registra
 tion or at the start of the program.Drop Off Program – This program is
  intended for children over the age of 6 years who can participate indepen
 dently. Adult(s) must be present to check in child with youth services sta
 ff prior to program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center C
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/lego-block-party-172194
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
