UID:b1c71b7bc6fce83b3427950d89997088@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nBest for grades 3
 -5.  Join the Master Gardeners to learn about pollination! After reviewing
  some of the basics of the pollination process\, we will dissect a lily fl
 ower and examine the reproductive parts of this plant.  We will also compa
 re insect vision with human vision and look at why the color and form of f
 lowers play a part in their attractiveness to insects.
LOCATION:Quarryville\, QVL C.X. Carlson Cultural Room
