SUMMARY:Teen Video Gaming: Super Smash Bros
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260624T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260624T160000
UID:d43d5beba8319080220d67a22036c858@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Gaming\, Summer Reading\, Teens\n\nGet ready to brawl! Join us
  for an epic Super Smash Bros. Ultimate Tournament on the Nintendo Switch\
 , where teens battle it out for bragging rights and prizes. Whether you're
  a seasoned fighter or a casual button-masher\, this tournament is open to
  all skill levels. Come solo or bring your crew—only one will be crowned
  Smash Champion!We’ll kick things off with warm-up rounds\, then dive in
 to a bracket-style tournament with 1v1 matches on the big screen. Between 
 matches\, enjoy snacks\, cheer on your friends\, and hang out in a chill\,
  gamer-friendly space.Registration for Teen Video Gaming: Super Smash Bros
 . will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 10th for Manheim Township and Ea
 st Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, June 17th for residents of other 
 municipalities.Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to canc
 el their registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be 
 restricted from registering for future programs for a period of one month
 ’s time. Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the 
 start of the program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notified
  of their change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10
  minutes prior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other 
 circumstances. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At 
 this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will
  be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the p
 rogram. However\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5
  minutes past the start time.Drop Off Program – This program is intended
  for children over the age of 13 years who can participate independently. 
 Adult(s) must be present to check in child with youth services staff prior
  to program. Adults will not be allowed in the event space. Check In - All
  participants must provide an emergency contact number upon registration o
 r at the start of the program.Designated Ages – Please adhere to the a
 ge restrictions designated on your registration. Only children in that age
  range will be admitted.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center C
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-video-gaming-super-
 smash-bros-175094
