DESCRIPTION:Arts & Crafts\, Community\, Discussion\, Health & Wellness\, M
 usic\, STEM\, Storytime\, Summer Reading\, Babies\, Toddlers\, Children\, 
 Tweens\, Teens\, Adults\, Seniors\, Everyone\n\nImagine a fun-filled short
  trip to West Africa to play drums\, dance\, sing\, learn\, and SMILE\, al
 l at your favorite library! This program with Tammi will have you dancin
 ’ on your feet and movin’ in your seat.  Let’s go back in time and l
 earn about the original story of The Lion King…but this time\, you are i
 n it\, playing rhythms with your hands and stomping with your feet. Drums 
 are provided\, but bring your favorite percussion instrument if you have o
 ne!It will be an honor and a fun experience to take part in this unique dr
 umming experience!
LOCATION:Manheim Community\, MAN Kreider Cultural Center
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/intergenerational-drum-c
 lass-172330
