SUMMARY:Mini-Archeologists: Discover Ancient Greece
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260706T153000
UID:aafcc980a1c6fce21de436d176d0df3b@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Storytime\, Children\n\nStep into the role of a young e
 xplorer at Mini Archaeologist Academy! In this hands-on program series jun
 ior archaeologists will investigate ancient civilizations\, uncover hidden
  artifacts and learn how archaeologists discover clues about the past thro
 ugh fun activities and crafts! In this session we’ll travel back in time
  to Ancient Greece to explore temples\, pottery and famous myths. Kids wil
 l discover ancient artifacts\, design their own Greek-style pottery and le
 arn about the stories and symbols that were important in Greek culture thr
 ough games and activities! Ages 6-9.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH 1/2 Multipurpose Room Projector Side
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/mini-archeologists-disco
 ver-ancient-greece-166007
