SUMMARY:Teen Advisory Board
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T190000
UID:9db2cb2f80746283ad62fb459a70a692@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Teens\n\nAre you a teen who loves the library and 
 wants to make a difference? Join our Teen Advisory Board—a new leadershi
 p opportunity for teens to shape library programs\, services\, and spaces!
 As a member\, you’ll:📚 Help plan and promote exciting teen events💡
  Provide input on books\, technology\, and programs you want to see🎤 De
 velop leadership skills and gain volunteer experience🤝 Make friends and
  connect with your communityWe’re looking for passionate\, creative\, an
 d motivated teens (ages 13 - 18) who want to have a voice in making the li
 brary an awesome place for young people.Meetings: Once a month at the libr
 aryPerks: Gain leadership experience\, make an impact\, and if you choose 
 to become a library volunteer\, you can earn volunteer hours!Program Polic
 iesDrop Off Program – This program is intended for children over the age
  of 13 years who can participate independently. Adult(s) must check in wit
 h library staff to provide an emergency contact at their first meeting. Ad
 ults will not be allowed in the event space. Designated Ages – Please ad
 here to the age restrictions designated on your registration. Only childre
 n in that age range will be admitted.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Study Room #119
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/teen-advisory-board-1569
 41
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/learning-robotics-arts-and-crafts-178704"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Learning Robotics with Arts and Crafts
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260713T193000
UID:cf6df002706e2c4c036acd4af5f370b3@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:STEM\, Summer Reading\, Tweens\n\nLearning Robotics with Arts 
 and Crafts for ages 10-14This arts and crafts program combines creativity 
 with engineering as participants explore basic robotics through hands-on p
 rojects. Participants will develop problem-solving skills\, ignite their c
 uriosity\, and gain an introductory understanding of robotics—all within
  a fun and creative environment. The program provides practical experience
  in constructing robotic creations and lays a foundation for future explor
 ation and potential careers in the dynamic\, rapidly evolving field of rob
 otics. Participants will also have an opportunity to drive one of our robo
 ts and learn more about FIRST robotics programs. We'll have new projects\,
  so past participants are encouraged to join us again.This program is led 
 by FIRST Tech Challenge Team 25650 - One Small Step for an Axolotl\, an al
 l-girls robotics team that won the 2026 Pennsylvania State Championship an
 d earned recognition at the FIRST World Championship. Girls are especially
  encouraged to participate!Please note: Projects will be similar to those 
 from the 2025 Summer Robotics Camp.Registration for Learning Robotics with
  Arts and Crafts will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, June 24th for Manheim 
 Township and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, July 1st for resid
 ents of other municipalities.Cancellations- Please check your email prior 
 to departing to verify that the program has not been cancelled. Library Pr
 ogram PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their registration for
  more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricted from registeri
 ng for future programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel y
 our registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to al
 low for those on the waiting list to be notified of their change in regist
 ration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the star
 t of the program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program
  will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will
  be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spot
 s remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registra
 nts will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start ti
 me.Drop Off Program – This program is intended for children over the age
  of 6 years who can participate independently. Adult(s) must be present to
  check in child with youth services staff prior to program. Adults will no
 t be allowed in the event space. Designated Ages – Please adhere to the 
 age restrictions designated on your registration. Only children in that ag
 e range will be admitted.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center C
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/learning-robotics-arts-a
 nd-crafts-178704
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
