 re programs for a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registr
 ations at least 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow those o
 n the waiting list to be notified of their change in registration status. 
 Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the
  program to allow for parking and other circumstances. The program will be
 gin promptly at the designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forf
 eited to those on the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain
 \, registrants may be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will
  not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time. 
 Drop Off Program – This program is intended for children over the age 
 of 6 years who can participate independently. Adult(s) must be present to 
 check in child with youth services staff prior to program. Adults will not
  be allowed in the event space.  *For children ages 6–7\, this is a 
 drop-off program\; however\, a parent or caregiver must remain nearby an
 d wait outside the program room for the duration of the program. Cancell
 ations- Please check your email prior to departing to verify that the prog
 ram has not been cancelled. Designated Ages – Please adhere to the age
  restrictions designated on your registration. Only children in that age r
 ange will be admitted.   Photography - The Manheim Township Public Lib
 rary Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing or video recording ind
 ividuals (including children) without their consent (or in the case of a c
 hild\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
