SUMMARY:Live STEAM Demo with the Railroad Museum of PA
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260805T113000
UID:3c999a73705825f73c7db5d9dd624196@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\n\nRegistration for Live STEAM Demo 
 presented by the Railroad Museum of Pennsylvania will open at 9:00AM on We
 dnesday\, July 22nd for Manheim Township and East Lampeter residents and o
 n Wednesday\, July 29th for residents of other municipalities.Registration
  Requirements –  To help us manage our space\, please register every per
 son who will be attending\, including adults or siblings.All aboard for a 
 high-energy journey through the science of trains! In this live STEAM (Sci
 ence\, Technology\, Engineering\, Art\, and Math) demonstration\, the Rail
 road Museum of Pennsylvania will fire up a working miniature steam engine 
 to show how steam power set the world in motion.With fascinating historic 
 artifacts\, dramatic photos\, and cool visual aids\, participants will unc
 over the evolution of locomotion—from the hissing power of steam to the 
 quiet force of electricity and the modern might of diesel-electric engines
 . It’s a fast-paced\, hands-on look at how trains helped shape the world
 —and the science that keeps them moving!Ideal for school-age children (A
 ges 7-12) and their families\, this program is perfect for curious minds w
 ho love trains\, history\, and hands-on learning.*For the safety and super
 vision of all participants: Children under 8 years old must be accompanied
  by an adult throughout the program. Children ages 8 and older are welcome
  to attend the program independently.  Library Program PoliciesNo Show –
  Patrons failing to cancel their registration for more than 2 library prog
 rams in a month will be restricted from registering for future programs fo
 r a period of one month’s time. Please cancel your registrations at leas
 t 2 hours prior to the start of the program to allow for those on the wait
 ing list to be notified of their change in registration status.Late Arriva
 ls – Please arrive 10 minutes prior to the start of the program to allow
  for parking and other circumstances. The program will begin promptly at t
 he designated time. At this time\, your spot will be forfeited to those on
  the wait list who will be granted entry. If spots remain\, registrants ma
 y be allowed into the program. However\, registrants will not be permitted
  to enter the program 5 minutes past the start time.Photography The Manhei
 m Township Public Library Code of Conduct Policy prohibits photographing o
 r video recording individuals (including children) without their consent (
 or in the case of a child\, the consent of a parent or guardian).
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center B
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/live-steam-demo-railroad
 -museum-pa-166987
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
