SUMMARY:Ed Klein: Flip Books for Youth
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260813T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260813T113000
UID:9ef8c5f1200309b6be4c27f5aa6d13d8@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Summer Reading\, Children\, Tweens\n\nRegistration for "Flip B
 ooks for Youth" will open at 9:00AM on Wednesday\, July 29th for Manheim T
 ownship and East Lampeter residents and on Wednesday\, August 5th for resi
 dents of other municipalities.This program is for children ages 8-12.Descr
 iption: Ever wondered how drawings come to life in the movies? Before Pixa
 r and special effect\, animated movies were made like a flip book! In this
  hands-on class\, join our master cartoonist\, Ed Klein\, who previously w
 orked with Hanna Barbera creating some of the most beloved cartoons! Parti
 cipants will discover how simple images\, when viewed in rapid sequence\, 
 bring the illusion of movement. Perfect for creative kids who love drawing
  or storytelling\, this program combines art\, imagination\, and a little 
 movie magic to bring characters to life- one page at a time!Presenter: As 
 an active artist in the field of animation\, Ed has contributed to over th
 ree hundred television commercials\, five full-length animated feature fil
 ms\, and numerous animated television specials and educational films. As a
 n active cartoon character artist and designer\, Ed has designed and illus
 trated toys\, games\, apparel\, jewelry\, and figurines for The Warner Bro
 s. Studio Stores\, and The Disney Stores\, as well as for independent lice
 nsees.Library Program PoliciesNo Show – Patrons failing to cancel their 
 registration for more than 2 library programs in a month will be restricte
 d from registering for future programs for a period of one month’s time.
  Please cancel your registrations at least 2 hours prior to the start of t
 he program to allow for those on the waiting list to be notified of their 
 change in registration status.Late Arrivals – Please arrive 10 minutes p
 rior to the start of the program to allow for parking and other circumstan
 ces. The program will begin promptly at the designated time. At this time\
 , your spot will be forfeited to those on the wait list who will be grante
 d entry. If spots remain\, registrants may be allowed into the program. Ho
 wever\, registrants will not be permitted to enter the program 5 minutes p
 ast the start time.Drop Off Program – This program is intended for child
 ren over the age of 8 years who can participate independently. Adult(s) mu
 st be present to check in child with youth services staff prior to program
 . Adults will not be allowed in the event space. Designated Ages – Pleas
 e adhere to the age restrictions designated on your registration. Only chi
 ldren in that age range will be admitted.
LOCATION:Manheim Township\, MTP Morgan Center A
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/ed-klein-flip-books-yout
 h-162387
