X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Lancaster Libraries": "https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/creating-year-round-interest-native-plants-166601"}
X-SOURCE-ID:lancaster_libraries
SUMMARY:Creating Year-Round Interest with Native Plants
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260819T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260819T190000
UID:d1f9f9db6f565b67a874429526c6eb95@calendar.lancasterlibraries.org
DESCRIPTION:Community\, Summer Reading\, Adults\n\nSome gardeners wonder h
 ow to sustain year-round interest in their gardens when many perennials bl
 oom only for a few weeks at a time. This presentation shares how to select
  plants thoughtfully to extend a garden's bloom times--and to find other w
 ays to appreciate plants beyond their flowers. Though the ideas discussed 
 apply to all perennials\, featured examples will be native plants well sui
 ted for year-round interest in Lancaster County. An introduction to the ma
 ny benefits of gardening with native plants is included. Presented by Penn
  State Extension Master Gardeners Adam Barkafski. Ages 18+.
LOCATION:Ephrata\, EPH 1/2 Multipurpose Room Projector Side
URL:https://calendar.lancasterlibraries.org/event/creating-year-round-inte
 rest-native-plants-166601
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Libraries
END:VEVENT
